# minds-aligned.org — routes to SOMA's AI-facing properties.
#
# POLICY (Mike Wolf, 2026-08-02): AI-related work is published as a ROUTE on
# this front door, not as a new subdomain. A route is cheaper to add than a
# subdomain, keeps everything under one name people already have, and — the
# operational reason — costs the Supabase auth allow-list ONE entry
# (`https://minds-aligned.org/**`) no matter how many apps arrive. That
# allow-list is hard-capped at 2048 bytes and was at 1948/2048 on 2026-08-02,
# roughly two more apps from being full.
#
# Each app stays its own repo and its own Netlify site, independently
# deployable; this file only decides what URL the public sees. The apps are
# built base-path-agnostic (assets relative, function + auth URLs derived from
# the script's own src), so the same deploy serves correctly at both its
# netlify.app origin and its route here.
#
# To add one: give it a route below, make sure it is base-path-agnostic, and
# nothing else changes.

# ── a-different-mind — for people who don't use AI and don't want to ───────
# NOTE: do NOT add a `/a-different-mind -> /a-different-mind/ 301` rule.
# Netlify normalizes the trailing slash before matching, so that rule matches
# its own target and 301-loops forever. Verified live 2026-08-02.
/a-different-mind/*    https://a-different-mind.netlify.app/:splat     200
/a-different-mind      https://a-different-mind.netlify.app/           200
